[ … ]
First off, notice how the write-side critical section is protected not by RCU but via a regular spinlock (we
talked about this; RCU has no way to protect concurrent writers, and they must ensure some protection
themselves). Next, we use the RCU-safe version of list_add_tail(), called list_add_tail_rcu(), to
append a node to the tail of the list. Its comment is instructive as well:
