Exercise
Make a copy of the ch13/3_lockfree/list_demo_rcu/list_demo_rcu.c module’s code. Refactor it to
allow passing a module parameter buggy; when passed and set to 1, have the module issue a blocking
call in the RCU read-side critical section. See what happens; study the kernel log.
More RCU usage examples
Another, and a better, example of using basic RCU primitives is something we cover soon, in the
upcoming Fixing it – take 2: use RCU section. There, we solve concurrency issues when iterating over
all threads in the kernel task list, using RCU for lock-free synchronization. Ensure you check out the
code and try it out!
An even better example of using RCU primitives for a list-based module can be found here: https://
github.com/jinb-park/rcu_example/tree/master. Do check it out.
The next section shows you where you can access (much) more RCU documentation and, within it,
learn about in-kernel RCU usage.
