Furthermore, finding which particular lock was double-acquired is easy; look up the code of the
task_lock() routine:
// include/linux/sched/task.h */
static inline void task_lock (struct task_struct *p)
{
spin_lock(&p->alloc_lock);
}
So, it all makes perfect sense now; it’s a spinlock within the task structure named alloc_lock, just as
lockdep informed us (see Figure 13.21).
